Package: pdactrace
Type: Package
Title: Stage-Aware PDAC Atlas and Prospectively Frozen Tissue-to-Serum
    Biomarker Audit Framework
Version: 0.99.23
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Jibeom", family = "Ko",
           email = "rhwlqja1779@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-8630-1973")))
Description: pdactrace implements a transparent, deterministic
    claim-audit framework for stage-aware pancreatic ductal
    adenocarcinoma (PDAC) tissue-to-blood biomarker evidence. It
    integrates per-stage trajectory matching across bulk RNA-seq,
    tissue proteomics, single-cell origin, serum proteomics, and
    pancreatitis context, with explicit anchor-enrichment evaluation
    against a curated external reference set. The framework comprises
    a 12-template competitive trajectory catalog, a 3-axis + 2-gate
    reference score, an Evidence Math layer, TRACE-D tissue-to-serum
    directional evidence concordance, claim-tier classification, and
    weight-robustness and Pareto support audits. A prespecification
    layer supports freezing candidate scores, directions and a
    decision rule under a content hash before outcome labels are
    opened, with a distinct inconclusive terminal state when a frozen
    gate fails. Scope is deliberately PDAC-specific: the bundled atlas,
    the anchor reference set and every validated claim are PDAC, and no
    result is claimed for any other disease. Separately, no supervised
    classifier is trained or shipped, because validated non-circular
    early-detection ground truth is unavailable in PDAC.
